  "verbalization": "Nupharolutine appears to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through multiple pathways, all leading to the same target, COLO-824. This suggests that Nupharolutine may act as a common modulator of the polycomb group (PcG) complex, which is involved in gene regulation and cellular differentiation. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Nupharolutine targets COLO-824, which in turn is a target of several compounds, including (3S,3aR,4aS,6aR,7R,9aS,9bS)-Decahydro-7-[(1R,4Z)-6-methoxy-1,5-dimethyl-6-oxo-4-hexen-1-yl]-6a,9a-dimethyl-3-(1-methylethenyl)-1H-cyclopenta[a]cyclopropa[e]naphthalene-3a(4H)-propanoic acid, dehydro-gamma-sanshool, and 6Alpha,7Alpha-Dihydroxyannonene. These compounds are all known to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, implying that Nupharolutine may share a similar mechanism of action, potentially inhibiting the PcG complex and affecting gene expression. The consistent targeting of COLO-824 across different compounds supports a mechanistic link between Nupharolutine and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though further validation with direct interaction studies or in vivo experiments would be necessary to confirm this relationship.",
